Package: pmvalsampsizepexa
Title: Sample Size for Prediction Model Validation - ModelsCloud Wrapper
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ramin", "Rezaeianzadeh", email = "raminrzn@student.ubc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Joie", "Ensor", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the pmvalsampsize package this wrapper calls"),
    person("Richard D.", "Riley", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the validation sample size criteria"))
Description: A ModelsCloud wrapper for the 'pmvalsampsize' package, which
    computes the minimum sample size required to externally validate an
    existing multivariable clinical prediction model using the criteria of
    Riley et al. (2021) <doi:10.1002/sim.9025> and Archer et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.8766>. Supports continuous, binary and survival outcomes.
    The methodology and its implementation live in 'pmvalsampsize'; this
    package only adapts the calling convention to ModelsCloud (model_run(),
    get_sample_input(), get_default_input()) and adds the gateway entry point
    the platform dispatches to.
